<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46769" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠθμοειδής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>like a strainer,
			perforated</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hero
				<u>Spir.</u>
				1.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.699a
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κοιλίαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Aret.
					<u>SD</u>
					2.3
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἠ. ὀστοῦν</span> the
			<i>ethmoid</i> or <i>perforated</i> bone at the root of the
			nose, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>UP</u>
				11.12
			</span></i>: more freq. in pl., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ
			-ειδῆ</span>, with or without <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὀστᾶ</span>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				8.7
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἠ. δεξαμεναί</span>, of the
			kidneys, prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Ph.
				2.244
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱμο-, ἰσθμο-</span> codd., cf.
				<i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				<u>Nat.Fac.</u>
				1.15
			</span></i>). Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-δῶς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
					<u>Anat.</u>
					52
				</span></i>
			.</div>
